.Dd June 15, 2026
.Dt DMESG 1
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm dmesg
.Nd print the kernel message buffer
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints the contents of the kernel message ring buffer, which holds the
boot-time and runtime diagnostic output produced by the kernel
.Fn kprintf
path.
The buffer is a fixed-size circular buffer; once full, the oldest
messages are overwritten.
.Pp
The log is read from
.Pa /proc/kmsg ,
a read-only, non-consuming procfs file, so repeated invocations of
.Nm
all see the same (current) buffer contents.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl V
Print the program version and exit.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /proc/kmsg
The kernel message ring buffer.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ps 1
.Sh HISTORY
A native
.Nm
appeared in Substrate.
